{
  "kanji": "稲",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 稲\ntitle: rice plant\njlpt: 1\ntags: [jlpt-n1, grade-8, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 14\nradical: 禾\nradicalNumber: 115\nonyomi: [トウ, テ]\nkunyomi: [いね, いな-]\nquizOnyomi: [トウ]\nquizKunyomi: [いね, いな-]\ndistractors: [移, 秒, 秋]\n---\n\n# 稲 — rice plant\n\n**Strokes:** 14 · **Key (radical):** 禾 (no. 115) · **JLPT:** N1 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n稲 names the **rice plant**, not a bowl of cooked rice. Compare [稲](../words/稲.md) いね, the plant, with [米](../words/米.md) こめ, rice as grain, and [ご飯](../words/ご飯.md) ごはん, cooked rice or a meal.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology:** Find 禾 on the left and the claw-like strokes above 旧 (a vertical stroke to the left of 日) on the right. Imagine a hand inspecting rice plants. This is a visual memory aid, not a historical explanation.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| トウ | on | [水稲](../words/水稲.md) すいとう - rice grown in flooded paddies; an agriculture term |\n| テ | on, source-only here | Preserved from KANJIDIC2; no verified lexical example is supplied here |\n| いね | kun | [稲](../words/稲.md) いね - rice plant |\n| いな- | kun, bound form | [稲穂](../words/稲穂.md) いなほ - an ear or head of rice; いな- supplies the rice-plant part |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [稲](../words/稲.md) いね - rice plant\n- [稲穂](../words/稲穂.md) いなほ - ear or head of rice\n- [水稲](../words/水稲.md) すいとう - wetland rice; agriculture vocabulary\n\n## Notes\n\n- Learn いね as the independent noun and いな- in whole words such as いなほ. The dash marks a bound form; it is not pronounced.\n- [穂](穂.md) ほ names a grain-bearing head, a part of the plant rather than the whole plant.\n- [移](移.md), shift or transfer, [秒](秒.md), a second of time, and [秋](秋.md), autumn, share 禾 but have different right-hand shapes and meanings.\n- The source-only テ remains visible for lookup but is not selected for reading questions. Full metadata is preserved.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project), 2026-11-02 snapshot. Word families: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1167820, 1167920, 1371310, 1508750 and 1270590.\n",
